{"id":1356,"date":"2021-06-24T09:04:38","date_gmt":"2021-06-24T09:04:38","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/?post_type=rdrcnews&#038;p=1356"},"modified":"2021-06-24T17:55:22","modified_gmt":"2021-06-24T17:55:22","slug":"art-culture-in-downtown-far-rockaway","status":"publish","type":"rdrcnews","link":"https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/rdrcnews\/art-culture-in-downtown-far-rockaway\/","title":{"rendered":"Art &#038; Culture In Downtown Far Rockaway"},"content":{"rendered":"<p><span style=\"color: #b87614;\">Downtown Far Rockaway Artist Commissioning Program<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000080;\">RDRC\/QCA Storefront Improvement Program; funded by NYC Small Business Services, Neighborhood 360 Grant, a community art commissioning project focused on placing temporary artwork designed by a local artist on the solid rolldown gates located in Downtown Far Rockaway. Our Queens Local Artists: Stanislava Ivanova, Brandi Jones, Brendan McInerney, and Shenna Vaughn.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000080;\">RDRC&#8217;s Downtown Far Rockaway Artists Commissioning Storefront\/Improvement Program; a democratized art commissioning project focused on placing temporary artwork designed by a local artist on solid rolldown gates located in Downtown Far Rockaway. The project funded by <span style=\"color: #b87614;\"><a class=\"editor-rtfLink\" style=\"color: #b87614;\" href=\"https:\/\/www1.nyc.gov\/site\/sbs\/neighborhoods\/storefront-improvement.page#:~:text=The%20program%20reimburses%20up%20to,or%20before%20September%2030%2C%202020.\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">the New York City Department of Small Business Services (NYC SBS)<\/a><\/span>\u00a0is a partnership with RDRC &amp; Queens Council on the Arts (QCA), designed for Downtown Far Rockaway businesses, property owners, and local artist&#8230;<span style=\"color: #b87614;\"><a class=\"editor-rtfLink\" style=\"color: #b87614;\" href=\"https:\/\/drive.google.com\/file\/d\/1EuksUHajhhh7HnE3Jj7vIhWjvRgdFQ6X\/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">more<\/a><\/span>.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000080;\">Storefront Improvement Program essential to upgrading; enhancing, and creating a well-designed storefront attracting customers; highlighting local businesses; defining the community and promoting a thriving neighborhood, bringing more visibility and identity to the character of Downtown Far Rockaway.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000080;\"><strong>Click <span style=\"color: #b87614;\"><a style=\"color: #b87614;\" href=\"https:\/\/www.facebook.com\/rockawaydevrevcorp\/photos\/pcb.958544414994138\/958542534994326\">here<\/a><\/span>, to see completed Art Work by Shenna Vaughn, artists assigned to Queens Defenders, located at 1922 Mott Avenue, Far Rockaway, NY&#8230;by Shenna Vaughn&#8230;follow her on Instagram<\/strong> <span style=\"color: #b87614;\"><a style=\"color: #b87614;\" href=\"https:\/\/www.instagram.com\/shennavaughn\/?hl=en\">@shennavaughn<\/a><\/span><\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000080;\">Community Panelist experienced cultural professionals committed to developing the arts and culture in their Queens community. Each QCA panelist knows Queens communities and expertise in an artistic discipline, arts administration, or community arts programming.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000080;\">The artists chosen presented a fresh perspective by creating work that speaks to the cultural diversity of Downtown Far Rockaway Queens by bringing a more vibrant and welcoming feel to our Rockaway community. As the Rockaway community undergoes revitalization and challenges due to COVID-19, the community continues to grow. The need to further enhance the communities&#8217; economic growth through neighborhood promotions and financial resources for public improvements.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000080;\">To learn more about our partner Queens Council on the Arts (QCA), click\u00a0<a class=\"editor-rtfLink\" style=\"color: #000080;\" href=\"https:\/\/www.queenscouncilarts.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span style=\"color: #b87614;\">here<\/span><\/a>.\u00a0\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"color: #000080;\">The CBO&#8217;s website is the primary source of news in the Downtown Far Rockaway neighborhood. It provides information on community happenings, business opportunities, invitations, and information on our programs and services. Join our\u00a0<span style=\"color: #b87614;\"><a class=\"editor-rtfLink\" style=\"color: #b87614;\" href=\"https:\/\/visitor.r20.constantcontact.com\/manage\/optin?v=001f-KEXzn5tO1N9oJq961YEq-GzWV1xAIboWtxqYSZXpq5yO1UUgfaSniqtf1xswR-A8b9vOUVS7HXpQIU0guJvspmnPOyroO7_bzKHe449Dw%3D\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">weekly electronic newsletter<\/a><\/span>\u00a0for upcoming happenings and business resources; subscribers will also receive periodic invites to special RDRC events.<\/span><\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Downtown Far Rockaway Artist Commissioning Program RDRC\/QCA Storefront Improvement Program; funded by NYC Small Business Services, Neighborhood 360 Grant, a community art commissioning project focused on placing temporary artwork designed by a local artist on the solid rolldown gates located in Downtown Far Rockaway. Our Queens Local Artists: Stanislava Ivanova, Brandi Jones, Brendan McInerney, and [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"featured_media":1357,"parent":0,"menu_order":0,"template":"","meta":{"_acf_changed":false},"class_list":["post-1356","rdrcnews","type-rdrcnews","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry"],"acf":[],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/rdrcnews\/1356","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/rdrcnews"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/www.rdrc.org\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/rdrcnews"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/w